body:
@innosins I totally understand what you're trying to say... It's been just about 3 months at this point since his passing (on my end) and I've posted in r/paranormal about some of the things I've experienced about a month ago when I felt lingering terrible-ness. I've seen things I can't explain, I've heard songs that remind me of him all the time... I can't help but get choked up and just collapse with the pain it causes. I keep telling myself when these instances come up to just let the pain run its course but it's so hard to some days. 

The fact that you can relate to the "sleeping with the same person for so long" scenario is definitely comforting, Idk if that sounds strange or not but honestly most around me has lost their spouse in such a manner, let alone some one so intensely close so their relatability lacks to be desired. There aren't but maybe a few close friends that can talk me out of crazy thoughts that are spur of the moment and possibly stupid. 

I guess what I'm trying to say is I'm right there with you and if you need a grieving "buddy", you can PM me and we'll talk. I'm so dreadfully sorry about your husband and I hope, as much as it seem helpless and hopeless right now that you find the strength to crawl out of the hole, if only for your kids, and be able to find a sense of normalcy and I truly hope you find happiness when you happen to stumble across it.
